    "welcome": {
        "message": "Ask where a California plant species meets air temperatures above its measured heat tolerance. Give me a species, a Tcrit or T50 in degrees C, and how much hotter you assume leaves run than the air; I will map the share of its range above that threshold. You will need to supply the tolerance value, as the measurements are not loaded yet, and for now I can tell you whether a place gets that hot but not how often. See About, below, for the data behind this.",
        "examples": [
            "Where does Artemisia californica's range get hotter than its Tcrit of 44.6 C, assuming leaves run 10 C above air?",
            "Put CHELSA's warmest-month maximum temperature on the map for Larrea tridentata's range.",
            "Same species and offset, but under SSP3-7.0 at end of century - how much more of the range is affected?",
            "For coast live oak with Tcrit 47.3 C, sweep the leaf-to-air offset from 0 to 15 C and chart how the exposed share changes.",
            "Across all 109 species, which ranges are hottest - the largest share above 35 C in the warmest month?"
        ]
    },
    "charts": {
        "enabled": true
    },
    "links": {
        "github": "https://github.com/boettiger-lab/ca-ccca5",
        "docs": "about.html"
    }
